{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/549575-examples-of-subverting-the-heroic-cycle","id":549575,"title":"Examples of Subverting the Heroic Cycle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-10T19:02:08-07:00","id":549575,"title":"Examples of Subverting the Heroic Cycle","content":"First, who the heck decided not to call this game Monster Manifesto? Just needed to get that off my chest. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Ok, so one of the neat things about this game is that the Antagonist faction is the archetypal square jawed Hero that has populated fiction from the Epic of Gilgamesh to Star Wars to Dr. Horrible's Sing-a-Long Blog. Leaving aside some of the nuances of the Heroes' portrayal in the current text, the idea of a personalized supervillain/nemesis is just awesome. Even better - the game challenges you the player (and Storyteller) to come up with ways to subvert the classic heroic cycle.<br /> <br /> The heroic cycle (as portrayed by Joseph Campbell) is pretty complex, but for the purposes of this post, the Heroic cycle in Beast will nearly always begin the same way:<ul><li>A monster ravages the countryside and the land calls out for blood.</li> <li>A Hero hears the call to adventure.</li> </ul>The standard way this story is resolved, at least according to Heroic culture is as follows:<ul><li>The Hero slays the monster.</li> <li>The Hero goes on to have more adventures.</li> </ul>The book offers two major ways to subvert this narrative resolution.<br /> <br /> 1. Inversion or Failure of the Heroic Quest<ul><li>The Monster through cunning or force slays the Hero.</li> <li>The Monster goes to have more adventures.</li> </ul>2. Abandonment of Adventure<ul><li>The Hero loses the urge to kill (gains Integrity 5).</li> <li>The Hero abandons the call to adventure and parts ways with the Monster.</li> </ul>I have a couple of other ideas:<br /> <br /> 3. Hate and Love are two sides of the same coin.<ul><li>The Hero and the Monster, after obsessing over each other for so long, come to respect (perhaps even love?) each other.</li> <li>The former Hero and the Monster go have adventures together.</li> </ul>4. &quot;You've just taken your first step into a much wider world (of darkness).&quot;<ul><li>The Hero comes to realize that there are worthier foes than their Monster.</li> <li>The Hero abandons their Nemesis to terrorize Mages, Werewolves, Changelings, Prometheans, and other unsuspecting beings.</li> <li>The Monster feels responsible and follows their former Nemesis trying to limit the Hero's war on all the &quot;... Sorcerers, Nightgaunts, Faerie, Boggies, Wytches, Dyvells, Changelings, Werebeasts, and all divers Creatures of the Night.&quot;</li> </ul>5. The Hero captures the Monster.<ul><li>The Hero survives the dangers of the Lair and subdues the slumbering Soul, but decides to keep it alive as a trophy.</li> <li>The Hero expels the powerless Monster from their own Lair.</li> <li>The Hero repurposes the Lair as a base from which to launch new assaults on new Lairs to steal more trophy souls.</li> <li>The Hero learns to create burrows between these subjugated Lairs and reigns supreme.</li> </ul>6. The Hero becomes the Monster.<ul><li>The Hero kills the Monster, but before the slumbering Soul can become Unfettered, the Hero grapples it in one final battle.</li> <li>The Hero looks into the maw of unrestrained Hunger and recognizes it. The Hero becomes the new Monster.</li> </ul>Any comments or additional ideas?<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I have been informed that &quot;slumbering&quot; (and not &quot;slumbering&quot;) is the term for when the Soul is at Satiety 10 and cannot merge with the Beast in the Lair. I've amended the post to reflect that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 06-11-2015, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T19:53:32-07:00","id":549612,"title":"","content":"A system where Heroes <i>become</i> Beasts sounds like something I would love -- there's so much story potential in that. If the Hero had Hunter buddies, how do they feel about this change -- if they know about it? If the former Hero falls in with a new Brood, how will they react? Balancing the old, Heroic life with this new Monstrous one without anyone finding out sounds like it could be fun -- and unlike Werewolf 2e, you have the potential of losing <i>both</i> sides hahahHAHAHAHA<br /> <br /> A captured Monster sounds like the beginning of someone else's story, too -- and Beasts do like to brag about being the origin of everything. Kind of picturing a Changeling crossover where, for instance, the Lindworm Prince is a Beast who was captured, eaten by the Hero's significant other, and reborn as the Hero's secret child or something like that. . .well, I'd have fun with it anyway. (And Donkeyskin starts out with a magic donkey who's ears drop gold coins when they're brushed, so you know. . . trophies. Heroes having kids and raising them around monsters could be fun backstory too)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T20:47:00-07:00","id":549717,"title":"","content":"I'm actually planning a setting based around #4 combined with a few &quot;side quests&quot; taken from the Hero's Journey RPG. I'm hoping that both will release around the same time so i can make heroic backgrounds that are derived from the actual Myths instead of a grab bag of delusions of grandeur. Heroes aren't meant to change; so it makes more sense to say &quot;he will always be x&quot; then &quot;This Hero hunts x, now he hunts y because he's more interested in them&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T20:57:37-07:00","id":549725,"title":"","content":"I would probably use this depending on the campaign but this destroys a lot of things beast is trying to do.<br /> <br /> Hate and Love are two sides of the same coin.<ul><li>The Hero and the Monster, after obsessing over each other for so long, come to respect (perhaps even love?) each other.</li> </ul>I see that working really well depending on how the hero or beast work but the problem is what if the hero took it personal like the one in the example where he pretty much attacked and killed one of her employees just because he thought he was a minion in his eyes what would if it wasn't just an employee what if it was someone close i.e family, friends. Same thing goes for beast as well<ul><li>The former Hero and the Monster go have adventures together.</li> </ul>Still depends on how they fought or their standpoints to each other.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;You've just taken your first step into a much wider world (of darkness).&quot;</span></span></span><ul><li>The Hero comes to realize that there are worthier foes than their Monster.</li> </ul>I can see that and would love to see how heroes work against vampires and mages and see if I can have them use their anathema powers against them.<ul><li>The Monster feels responsible and follows their former Nemesis trying to limit the Hero's war on all the &quot;... Sorcerers, Nightgaunts, Faerie, Boggies, Wytches, Dyvells, Changelings, Werebeasts, and all divers Creatures of the Night.&quot;</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">This one I can't see working because most of game was designed to be crossover friendly and to the beast they consider the supernatural world to be family and care about them why would they start a war against there own family.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Hero captures the Monster.</span></span></span><ul><li>The Hero survives the dangers of the Lair and subdues the sated Soul, but decides to keep it alive as a trophy.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">so what so it can escape? if you were to kill the beast while it was away from its soul it would not work unless said beast satiety was 10<ul><li>The Hero expels the powerless Monster from their own Lair.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">So why can't they take it back ? when a beast dies their lair is gone. Unless I am reading wrong then this would be an interesting.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Hero becomes the Monster.</span></span></span></span><ul><li>The Hero kills the Monster, but before the sated Soul can become Unfettered, the Hero grapples it in one final battle.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Like I said they don't become unfettered unless the beast has a satiety of 10<ul><li>The Hero looks into the maw of unrestrained Hunger and recognizes it. The Hero becomes the new Monster.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I stated that beast was crossover friendly and that they would not wage war against other supernatural they consider kin problem is you made it that other beast have a hard time trusting each other not. What if the nice Beast I met a minute ago was not some hero who wasted the real beast or if my sister who I know was a hero just suddenly became beast. That would make thing really hard for beasts to trust each other especially in the mind of the beast what if the heroes who became a beast is not done acting like a hero? basically you made it into demon the descent<br /> <br /> to be honest these are all interesting plot hooks that can be used but they also don't work concerning parts of the game.</span><br /> </span><br /> </span><br /> <br /> </span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:01:44-07:00","id":549731,"title":"","content":"I certainly admit that a lot of this clashes with the tone of certain parts of the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> However, I do want to clarify that I meant that the Hero started hunting mages, vampires, etc, and the Beast pursues the Hero to stop this destructive set of &quot;side quests.&quot; I intended that option as a hook for crossover. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, any time I use the term &quot;sated&quot;, I mean &quot;Satiety 10.&quot; I thought those terms were equivalent, but I might be wrong. <br /> <br /> I think my favorite idea I mentioned was the idea of a Hero capturing a sleeping/sated/satiety 10 soul, and kicking the powerless human/former Beast out. It's almost like an inverted Inheritance and could serve as a Big Bad for a group of Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 06-11-2015, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:10:18-07:00","id":549737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/549575-examples-of-subverting-the-heroic-cycle?p=549731#post549731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly admit that a lot of this clashes with the tone of certain parts of the game. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> However, I do want to clarify that I meant that the Hero started hunting mages, vampires, etc, and the Beast pursues the Hero to stop this destructive set of &quot;side quests.&quot; I intended that option as a hook for crossover. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, any time I use the term &quot;sated&quot;, I mean &quot;Satiety 10.&quot; I thought those terms were equivalent, but I might be wrong.<br /> <br /> I think my favorite idea I mentioned was the idea of a Hero capturing a sleeping/sated/satiety 10 soul, and kicking the powerless human/former Beast out. It's almost like an inverted Inheritance and could serve as a Big Bad for a group of Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok this makes more sense but what happens to the person he kicked out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 06-11-2015, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T01:40:04-07:00","id":549892,"title":"","content":"Satiety 10 is called &quot;Slumbering&quot;. &quot;Sated&quot; is already the name for satiety 4-6, so using it here could get confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T02:23:35-07:00","id":549915,"title":"","content":"Think you missed one Potential one...<br /> 7: &quot;Even Evil has Standards&quot;<ul><li>The &quot;Monster&quot; that the Hero is chasing Actively saves/rescues innocents the Hero has placed in Harms way</li> <li>The Beast shows the Hero who they really are and that they are MUCH Worse then them, convincing them to abandon the Hunt</li> <li>The &quot;Monster&quot; identifies the Hero as Kin and Welcomes them into the Family &quot;Here, This is my Cousin... She's Single&quot; Making them Question their Quest</li> </ul><br /> Could be afew others in that... but can't think of them off the top of my Head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T04:09:37-07:00","id":549953,"title":"","content":"I love these ideas! <br /> <br /> They exemplify the explorative aspect of Beast and I will definitly be encouraging my players to look beyond what's expected of them to change their character's narrative. In particular I had been toying around with a (albiet corney) Beauty and the Beast themed Inheritance that's essentially #3. Only difference was that the end result would put the Beast's Soul into a perminent slumber, essentially making them an ordinary human without the constant pangs of Hunger influencing their every action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T06:50:26-07:00","id":550059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/549575-examples-of-subverting-the-heroic-cycle#post549575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]The Hero and the Monster, after obsessing over each other for so long, come to respect (perhaps even love?) each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is your fault.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://th02.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/i/2014/042/1/d/tsundere_sharktastic_valentine_by_rainspeak-d762ptg.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T07:38:37-07:00","id":550101,"title":"","content"