&quot;. &quot;Sated&quot; is already the name for satiety 4-6, so using it here could get confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woops, thanks for the correction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/549575-examples-of-subverting-the-heroic-cycle?p=549915#post549915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think you missed one Potential one...<br /> 7: &quot;Even Evil has Standards&quot;<ul><li>The &quot;Monster&quot; that the Hero is chasing Actively saves/rescues innocents the Hero has placed in Harms way</li> <li>The Beast shows the Hero who they really are and that they are MUCH Worse then them, convincing them to abandon the Hunt</li> <li>The &quot;Monster&quot; identifies the Hero as Kin and Welcomes them into the Family &quot;Here, This is my Cousin... She's Single&quot; Making them Question their Quest</li> </ul><br /> Could be afew others in that... but can't think of them off the top of my Head.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the idea of Beasts getting their Family to function as a support group for repentant Heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"h